        <reimplements refid="class_a_g_e_1_1_index_buffer_1ae940c238a7a3ef8862c0f073645731d3">Bind</reimplements>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function binds the OpenGL Index <ref refid="struct_a_g_e_1_1_buffer" kindref="compound">Buffer</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function uses glBindBuffer to bind the buffer with ID &apos;m_RendererID&apos; as an element array buffer (GL_ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER). It is used for rendering of indexed primitives, such as triangles or lines, using vertices from a vertex array.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>void No return value.</para>
</simplesect>
This function binds the OpenGL Index <ref refid="struct_a_g_e_1_1_buffer" kindref="compound">Buffer</ref>.</para>
<para>It uses glBindBuffer to bind the buffer with target GL_ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER and the ID of this buffer as argument. The purpose of binding an index buffer is to specify which vertex array object (VAO) should be used for rendering. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
